$plugin->release   = '1.5.33'; // IMAP-DEEP-DIAGNOSTIC (v1.5.33 / 29 Jul 2026): Replaced the blind "Test IMAP" button with a deep diagnostic that tries BOTH username formats (strip_domain ON and OFF) and lists every folder with its message count. New per-student "Test Mailbox" button on every active row. The diagnostic shows exactly which format connects, which has messages, and gives a one-line fix recommendation (e.g. "Toggle strip_domain OFF — opposite format has 47 messages in INBOX"). New AJAX action: test_imap_student (takes userid param). Modal result panel shows: IMAP spec used, username sent, INBOX count, all folders + counts, and a colour-coded recommendation. Savepoint 2026072900221. // IMPORT-COLLISION-FIX: import_existing() now pre-builds an in-memory map of already-linked emails from SQL before the loop — skips any match that would violate the email_idx UNIQUE constraint instead of crashing. Wrapped save_account_record() in try/catch(\dml_exception) so a single DB error never aborts the whole import. Return value now includes skipped count + error list. DIAGNOSE-SQL: diagnose_import report now includes SQL queries showing (a) emails linked to 2+ users, (b) unlinked users with identical names (collision risk), (c) status breakdown of linked accounts. // CPANEL-LOCALPART-FIX: import_existing() cpanel_map now correctly extracts localpart from login/user/email fields regardless of whether cPanel returns login as bare localpart (older) or full email (v136+). DIAGNOSE-IMPORT: New diagnostic button opens a report showing raw cPanel API response, field names, old vs fixed localpart parsing, and Moodle candidate list — so the exact mismatch can be confirmed. // DATA-QUALITY: Data Quality Report modal in dashboard header — shows duplicate Moodle accounts (same name), multiple SEM records per user, orphaned records (user deleted), and suspended-Moodle/active-cPanel mismatches. AJAX action get_data_quality added. // IMPORT-MATCH-FIX: import_existing() now correctly extracts the localpart from email-style Moodle usernames (aiop2411022@aiopms.com.au → aiop2411022) before matching against cPanel accounts — previously the @ was stripped and the candidate became nonsense, causing every match to fail silently. // FILTER-DROPDOWN: Status filter dropdown added to dashboard search bar — filter by All / Not Linked / Active / Suspended / Archived / Error. Syncs bidirectionally with the stat card click-filters. // CLEAR-EXT-BADGE: reset_password() now clears the stale "Pwd externally managed" notes badge on success — whether triggered manually (Reset PW / Fix Missing Passwords) or auto-triggered by the mailbox client on first open. // AUTO-PW-ON-IMPORT: import_existing() and link_account() now auto-generate a new cPanel password, store it encrypted, and send welcome credentials immediately — no more "Pwd externally managed" limbo requiring a manual Reset PW step. // DEBUG-CONSOLE: Full F12 DevTools debugging — semDebug() styled JS logger on every AJAX send/receive; SMTP conversation (PHPMailer SMTPDebug=3) returned in JSON smtp_log field and printed to console; X-SEM-Step response headers show last PHP checkpoint reached; X-FATAL header surfaces PHP fatals in Network tab even when body is empty. // ONE-CLICK-LINK: Link Existing now fetches unlinked cPanel accounts into a dropdown — selecting one links instantly, no typing needed. Falls back to manual text entry if cPanel is unreachable or all accounts already linked. New AJAX action: list_cpanel_accounts. Savepoint 2026062700006. // // TEST-SMTP: Added 'Test SMTP' button to admin dashboard toolbar. Calls new test_smtp AJAX action which opens a real PHPMailer smtpConnect() to the configured host/port, authenticates with one active student account's credentials, and reports success or a detailed error message — no email is sent. Savepoint 2026062700005. // FIX-MAILBOX-GETCREDS: mailbox.php called get_credentials() which does not exist — renamed to get_account_for_user(). Savepoint 2026062700004. // MAILBOX-CLIENT: Native IMAP/SMTP email client built directly into Moodle. Students click "My Email" and get a full inbox — read, compose, reply, forward, delete, folder sidebar, unread badge, search. No iframe, no Roundcube redirect. Requires PHP imap extension + SMTP settings. New settings: mailbox_enabled, smtp_host, smtp_port, smtp_encryption. lib.php updated to route "My Email" nav link to mailbox.php when enabled. Savepoint 2026062700001. // BTN-HOVER-FIX: Fixed all button hover states — added colour:#fff on :hover for every white-text button (.btn-bulk, .btn-bulk-import, all .sem-btn variants); added text-decoration:none on <a>-based button hovers. Moodle/ITALC a:hover was overriding text to red. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026062600011. // DOUBLE-NAV-FIX: Wrapped dashboard external page and settings page under a shared admin_category so only one 'Student Email Manager' entry appears in Local Plugins (previously both the external page and settings page showed as separate identically-named entries). Dashboard lang string renamed from 'Student Email Manager' to 'Dashboard'. v1.2.2: ADMINLIB-FIX: require_once adminlib.php before admin_externalpage_setup() so dashboard.php no longer crashes with "Call to undefined function". v1.2.1: BUG FIX: (1) claim_next_number() now acquires a Moodle lock (core\lock\lock_config) before reading+incrementing the counter — previously two simultaneous enrolments could both read the same counter value and be assigned identical email addresses, causing a cPanel duplicate-account error. (2) encrypt_password() now uses a random 16-byte IV per encryption stored as v2:base64(iv+ciphertext), replacing the old static IV that produced identical ciphertext for identical passwords. Decrypt supports both v2 and legacy v1 format for backwards compatibility. v1.0.0 — Initial release. Auto-provisions cPanel mailboxes for Moodle students. UAPI first, JSON API v2 fallback. AES-256-CBC encrypted passwords, four email formats, admin dashboard, auto-rules on enrolment/suspension/deletion/reactivation, student My Email portal with Roundcube link.
